WEBVTT

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.190
I see.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:00.280
I thought you were acting cocky,
but that wasn't the case.

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:04.700
It's not that
you won't take your hands out,

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.460
it's that you can't.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.090
How unusual.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.100
You and I are facing the same way,

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.100
standing side by side.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.350
How long has it been?

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.100
Even in the ring,

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.110
something unusual is happening.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.360
It's Iai.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:55.630
Keeping your hands down
looks like a handicap at first glance.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:57.960
What a trickster.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.130
His stance looks careless at first,

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:05.140
<i>but it reaches the same speed</i>
<i>as when a sword is drawn.</i>

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:10.020
<i>Iai has the same force</i>
<i>hiding in that still-standing form.</i>

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.900
Just like the name implies,
it's the stance.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.900
That's right.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.400
Baki, learn from it.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:23.990
Even if

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.410
that technique will be used against you?

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.710
Cook it to perfection.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.750
Otherwise, I won't bite.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.170
This was a failure.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:42.930
I should have

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:47.010
done weight training on my eardrums too.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.440
You're finally looking at me directly.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.950
It's the Hand Pocket Stance!

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:10.950
This stance feels much better somehow.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.960
He's making fun of Ron!

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.460
Go Ron!

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.960
That's just like Oliva.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:24.760
This Hand Pocket Stance is nice.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.220
I like it.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.220
I should've done this from the start.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.480
His hands are out.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:42.240
Look at that.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.990
You stopped because
your opponent copied you.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.990
That's pretty small-minded.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.500
Why are your hands still inside?

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.250
You can't even counterattack.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.010
Aren't you able to pull your hands out?

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.390
Maybe I was too fast.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:12.640
Well, then...

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.270
What's wrong?

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.520
Counterattack if your hands are out.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:32.040
Here, try hitting me.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.830
You can hit my stomach at this distance.

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.540
You can even kick my balls.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:43.050
You can win in an instant.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:47.050
It's hopeless.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.140
Mr. Unchained is tied up.

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:03.440
I'll gladly do as you say.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:06.400
I believe in first-hand experience.

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:08.950
I'm an American, after all.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:13.030
Your punches can hit first,
even when your hands are pocketed?

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:17.710
I won't believe such mysterious bullshit.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:29.010
-All right!
-Amazing!

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:30.970
But he was at such a disadvantage.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.060
That idiot.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.980
Stop looking down on martial arts.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.770
I don't understand Iai Kenpo.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.650
The Hand Pocket Stance is a handicap,

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:46.480
yet he's still fast.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:49.320
That's why it's a technique.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.080
<i>At first glance,</i>
<i>he looks defenseless in that stance.</i>

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.080
<i>But he's already at the ready stance.</i>

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.630
<i>He doesn't pull out his fist</i>
<i>when he punches.</i>

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:07.420
<i>He forms his punch by swinging his hip</i>
<i>without repositioning his hand.</i>

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:11.380
<i>Thus, his opponent</i>
<i>can't see him pull it out.</i>

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:13.890
<i>He's properly prepared.</i>

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:17.890
<i>His fist is at full speed</i>
<i>while it's in the pocket.</i>

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:22.020
<i>Even if his opponent has their arms up,</i>

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:24.060
<i>he will never come late.</i>

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:25.690
<i>They will at least tie.</i>

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:30.780
That's why speed will never beat
a Kenpo user like Ron.

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:36.530
Shall I end it?

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:48.050
Now I get it.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:52.800
Your hand doesn't leave the pocket.

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:56.550
The pocket leaves your hand.

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:58.560
You can't see that.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:00.810
You can't beat that.

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:05.560
Don't challenge him,
keep to your strengths!

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:06.770
What?

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.820
Well, shall we begin?

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:20.450
The Hand Pocket Stance again?

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:21.660
Is he an idiot?

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.210
Ron is mad!

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:33.630
You're in such a hurry.

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:38.550
You wouldn't take out your hands for me.

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:41.720
You should slowly

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.730
and elegantly pull your hands out.

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:57.490
That's the stylish thing to do.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:08:59.700
The tables turned!

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.490
Oliva proved his willpower!

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:04.210
Ron was defeated by
the pocket hand technique.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.500
Don't be stupid.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:07.630
That's not a technique.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.090
That's not a skill.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:13.010
Idiot, skills and techniques mean nothing
if he won.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:14.510
He...

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:16.680
kept to his strengths.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.770
Ron stood up!

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:29.270
Hey. Good morning, Ron!

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:34.690
The Hand Pocket showdown is back!

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:37.200
An eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:40.030
A pocket for a pocket!

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:45.540
Your hand-pulling technique...

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:49.540
and my hand-pulling technique.

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:51.290
It's time...

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:53.050
to finish this.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:03.310
It's the Hand Pocket Stance again!

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:06.560
Right to the balls!

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.060
A consecutive kick!

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.360
It's a flurry of strikes!

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:20.950
Oliva hasn't defended himself...

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.120
for a while now.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.660
I told you, didn't I?

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:32.000
You're lacking...

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:33.210
My neck.

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:38.220
...a bit of style!

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:49.060
Right, Ron?

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:51.230
Am I wrong?

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:54.230
It's an Oliva headbutt to the face.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.980
I wouldn't want to feel that.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:05.740
A...

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:09.250
level-headed mind...

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:12.000
is invincible!

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:13.790
It's a counterattack!

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:15.500
Ron can still fight!

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:20.010
It's impossible.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:25.050
I don't know how much time you've spent

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:28.720
training that spear hand of yours.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:33.150
But when I harden my muscles for real,

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.520
it's better to give up.

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:43.070
For the likes of you to become strong,

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:46.870
I'm sure you went through
unimaginably hard training.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:50.580
<i>I go through my own kind of training too.</i>

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:52.210
<i>Countless times.</i>

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:55.130
<i>Countless times.</i>

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:13.020
He's punching with a broken hand.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:34.170
Damn, you just won't stop.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:38.340
We have a winner!

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.550
The Hand Pocket Stance,

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:45.430
even at the last moment.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:50.810
<i>He's a smart guy.</i>

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:10.950
Unchained.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:16.080
You finished it with a headbutt
to the face.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:19.460
That wasn't stylish at all.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:21.210
That hurts.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.720
We promised a perfect victory.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:30.390
But we start with a loss.

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:33.720
Maybe I was mistaken.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:39.480
We might be making enemies
with an outrageous bunch.

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.320
Master, if that's true,

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:48.570
what do you plan to do?

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:52.540
The remaining four matches

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.750
will all be fought by me.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:56.250
Master!

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:58.250
Shunsei.

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:00.170
Dad.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:04.920
You shouldn't take away toys
from your own kid.

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:07.510
Is that so?

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:10.010
One kill per person.

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:15.770
If the four of us slaughter them for
the rest of the matches, we'll look good.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:17.770
Those are big words.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:23.360
Do you want to die too?

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:26.110
I'm not your enemy.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:30.610
Very well.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:34.120
One kill per person.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.870
Make it happen, Shunsei.

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:40.920
Thanks, Dad.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:50.470
Let me tell you something.

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:53.600
Japan used to hold...

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:56.390
a tournament for underground martial arts.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:58.270
I'm sure you know.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:01.440
Yes, I've heard of it before.

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:02.770
So?

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:05.610
Your opponent in the upcoming match...

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:10.320
<i>was the champion.</i>

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:17.160
<i>Sympathy between two men</i>
<i>who have strong fathers.</i>

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:21.330
Begin!

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:24.500
<i>In any case,</i>
<i>one side has sprinted forward.</i>

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:32.840
<i>He dodges Shunsei's destructive punch</i>
<i>to the right side,</i>

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:36.640
<i>and strikes Shunsei's chin perfectly.</i>

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:40.100
<i>This makes his brain crash into his skull,</i>

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:43.020
<i>as if it were a pinball game.</i>

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.730
<i>The tremors cause the brain</i>
<i>to repeatedly crash into the skull,</i>

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:50.860
<i>creating typical concussion symptoms.</i>

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:54.110
<i>What's more,</i>

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:57.080
<i>he does a left uppercut</i>
<i>on Shunsei's lower jaw</i>

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:58.540
<i>for good measure.</i>

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.290
<i>Using his crumbling stance,</i>

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:05.630
<i>Baki does a left roundhouse kick.</i>

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:09.300
<i>This sends Shunsei</i>
<i>to a world far, far away,</i>

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:12.090
<i>ending everything.</i>

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:16.350
<i>This was only a two-second time frame.</i>

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:19.680
<i>The audience lost their voices,</i>

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:22.890
<i>and simply watched over</i>
<i>the situation before them.</i>

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:25.350
We have a winner!

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:31.320
<i>Baki Hanma, a boy who is soon</i>
<i>turning 18 years old.</i>

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:39.700
<i>He's in his best condition.</i>

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:49.210
You're stronger than your dad.

00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:53.010
You're amazing!

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.720
Truly amazing!

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:57.390
It's just as I thought.

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:00.720
You can guide Japan's young ones.

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:03.480
I what?

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.440
What do you think, Baki?

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:07.860
Would you like to join me?

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:23.500
Dad.

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:26.290
Hey, you.

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:31.000
Have you really inherited by blood?

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:37.090
Did I lose?

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:39.510
Amazing.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:42.470
That kid is a great fighter.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:47.690
Give up on martial arts.

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:53.780
-Hey, Baki.
-Yes?

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:56.780
Focusing on strength alone is boring.

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.030
Would you like to

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:03.540
use that strength to help others?

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:09.040
Jaku, you're amazing.

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:13.130
Despite your upcoming fight with that man,

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.050
you're still thinking about

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:18.800
guiding Japan's youth.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:22.550
You're strong.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:29.100
I wonder if someone at your age
understands such things.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:31.560
I was also...

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:33.020
I was also

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:36.070
able to become strong

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:38.320
for another's sake.

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:43.330
Retsu versus Jaku.

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:47.330
Who should I cheer for?

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:51.580
I won't lose.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:56.670
The current generation needs my victory.

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:01.590
I don't need to explain.

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:04.100
If you lose,

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:07.100
that marks our team's defeat.

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:12.810
I'm sure you're aware of
what that means for our 4,000 years

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:15.360
of Chinese martial arts history.

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:17.650
-Master.
-Yes?

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:21.360
I am ashamed by how much I still lack

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:26.240
because I feel very lucky

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:29.200
for ending up in this situation.

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.380
It's a critical moment
for the Chinese Allied Powers.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:36.000
There's no one to fall back on.

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:38.880
A single defeat will end it all.

00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:43.430
Gentle and tough,
a pure Japanese martial arts

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:46.140
Kukendo user, Sea King Jaku!

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:50.640
From the famous Bailin Temple,

00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:53.560
he's a man who lives up to his title.

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:55.770
It's Sea King Retsu!

00:19:56.980 --> 00:19:57.900
Begin!

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:03.910
Retsu.

00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:08.740
Let's at least start with this.

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:10.660
A handshake.

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:32.180
Bailin Temple.

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:34.190
Or rather...

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:37.690
Your famous title as
China's Sea King Retsu

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:40.690
is a thing of the past!

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:46.700
He got behind him!

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:48.700
He got his joints!

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:58.210
Jaku, that's dirty!

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:00.460
Coward, shame on you.

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:02.710
How wonderful.

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:05.720
No, this is truly wonderful.

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:10.810
Retsu.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:13.730
Let's form a team.

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:16.940
Reject him!

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:18.650
-I need you.
-What are you doing?

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.070
I need talent like you.

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:25.990
I knew for sure

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:28.490
that you'd grab my hand.

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:32.330
Sorry!

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:52.010
Amazing, Sea King Retsu!

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:54.520
How cowardly, Japan!

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:57.270
What cowardice!

00:21:57.730 --> 00:22:01.770
He uses a friendly handshake
to make a surprise attack!

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:04.070
This is an unforgivable act.

00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:10.280
He's a rare, despicable sneak.

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:12.870
What will you do, Sea King Retsu?

00:22:13.870 --> 00:22:16.290
How will you fight him, Sea King Retsu?

00:23:42.290 --> 00:23:43.210
IDIOTS FROM PLANET STRONG
